  "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z=0 \\\\ x+3y+z=-1 \\\\ 2x-3y-z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system above has the matrix representation $Ax=b.$ Given that $x=\u27e8x,y,z\u27e9$ is unique, what is the value of $\\frac{yz}{x}?$ \n\n*Hint: The inverse of the coefficient matrix is given by*\n\n$$\n\\,{A}^{-1}=-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -9 & 7 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
